note Translation of _parse_header_lines from CPython (Lib/http/client.py).
note Parses only RFC 5322 headers from header lines.
note
note email Parser wants to see strings rather than bytes.
note But a TextIOWrapper around self.rfile would buffer too many bytes
note from the stream, bytes which we later need to read as bytes.
note So we read the correct bytes here, as bytes, for email Parser
note to parse.

note GAP: a class passed as a value - `_class=HTTPMessage` lets the caller choose which Message subclass the parser builds. The doc has no type parameters on operations, no interfaces and no class values, so the result is fixed to HTTPMessage and the `_class` argument is dropped.
type HTTPMessage
    field headers as a List of Header

type Header
    field name as Text
    field value as Text

note GAP: there is no named text encoding in the doc. `decode ... as iso_8859_1` is a guess at the phrase. Latin-1 maps every byte to a character, so it cannot fail.
to decode bytes as iso_8859_1 using memory
    given bytes is Bytes
    given memory is an Allocator
    produces Text
    fails with OutOfMemory
    uses memory

note email.parser.Parser(_class=_class).parsestr(hstring). The Parser object is built and used once, so it is reduced to one operation.
to parse_message from text using memory
    given text is Text
    given memory is an Allocator
    produces an HTTPMessage
    fails with OutOfMemory
    uses memory

note GAP: no operation joins a list of Bytes. `join_bytes` is a guessed helper for b''.join.
to join_bytes parts using memory
    given parts is a List of Bytes
    given memory is an Allocator
    produces Bytes
    fails with OutOfMemory
    uses memory

note WORKAROUND: `_class` is a keyword argument with a default. Scribe has no defaults or keyword arguments, and no class values, so the parameter is removed rather than made required.
to parse_header_lines header_lines using memory
    given header_lines is a List of Bytes
    given memory is an Allocator
    produces an HTTPMessage
    fails with OutOfMemory
    uses memory

    let joined be try join_bytes header_lines using memory
    let hstring be try decode joined as iso_8859_1 using memory
    give back try parse_message from hstring using memory
